• i) **calculates** and **prints** the **maximum number of delegates** that can sit in the **8th** row.
• ii) **calculates** and **prints** the **number** of **consecutive rows** needed to seat **N** ($1 \le N \le 825$) delegates, **starting** from the **1st** row. The **number** of delegates **N** is given by the user; assume that it is given correctly and that no check is needed.

The program must display on the screen the appropriate messages for the data input and the output of the results, as in the example below:

### Example input (keyboard)

```input
83
```

### Example output (on the screen)

```output
Σύνεδροι 8ης σειράς:55
Δώσε πόσοι σύνεδροι:
Σειρές που χρειάζονται για να καθίσουν 83 σύνεδροι:4
```

(b) The program below, written in the C++ programming language, is given. Using the method of **dry run**, present the results of the program. In place of a space, use the symbol «□».

```C++
  #include<iostream>
  using namespace std;
  void calc(int x, int &y){
    if (x>0){
      x=y+3;
      y+=1;
    }
    else {
      x=3*y;
      y-=1;
    }
    cout<<"x="<<x<<" "<<"y="<<y<<endl;
  }
 int main(){
     int a=3,b=4,c=3;
